        <a href="{{ path('app_privacy_sms') }}">SMS Privacy Policy</a>; mobile opt-in data
        and phone numbers are not shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">9. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The Service relies on third-party providers, including Anthropic (AI analysis),
    Twilio (SMS), and email delivery. Their handling of data is governed by their own
    terms and policies.</p>

    <h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3" id="analytics">Analytics and cookies</h3>
    <p>On our public website we use Google Analytics 4 to understand how visitors find and
    use NouriLoop, so we can improve it. Analytics cookies are <strong>off by default</strong>
    and are only set if you choose &ldquo;Accept&rdquo; on our cookie banner; you can decline
    with no loss of functionality. We send Google only standard page views and a small set of
    named events (for example, creating an account or starting a subscription). <strong>We never
    send your health data, meals, metrics, or any personal content to analytics.</strong> The
    cookie that records your choice is a first-party cookie and contains only that preference.</p>
    <p>If you arrive from one of our ads, the link carries campaign labels in its web address
    (for example which ad campaign it belongs to). We keep those labels in your browser session
    and, if you go on to create an account, save them with your account so we can tell how many
    people each campaign brought us. We use them <strong>only as counts by campaign</strong>
    &mdash; never to build a profile of you, and they are never shared with anyone. This is
    entirely first-party: no third party is involved, and it does not depend on the analytics
    cookies described above.</p>
    <p>We also use the Meta Pixel (Facebook/Instagram) on our public, logged-out pages only
    &mdash; it is never loaded on any page that displays your health information, including
    your meals, health metrics, symptoms, trends, or insights. The one exception is the
    order-confirmation page shown right after you start a subscription, where it records only
    that single conversion. It is subject to the same opt-in cookie consent described above,
    and we send it only page views on public pages and the same named account/subscription
    events, never health data.</p>

